"Neurolash" or Neural Training Rod (Disrupting Neural Stimulator)

Core: The core of the Rod portion of the weapon consists of 24 semi-rigid disc-like objects that are 2.5 inches in diameter and 0.5 inches thick when it is fully collapsed. Within each of these disks is a dense non-Newtonian fluid that can solidify as a reaction to a number of different stimuli, which surrounds a central tube which contains sensitive electronics, wiring, and fluid transfer tubes. The semi-rigid exterior of these discs are made from a smart material similar to graphene but able to change size & shape. Linking each disc-like object to one another are a variety of smart materials & myomer cables which act sort of like ligaments, muscles, and tendons. This allows the individual discs to be moved or manipulated in a variety of manners much like a prehensile limb. 

Outer Layers: Sheathing both the disc-like objects and the linking segments is another thicker layer of highly durable & flexible graphene-like material that protects the core from damage, which is in turn surrounded by a layer of black rubber-like flexible material with a mesh much like Orthoskin embedded near the surface. This mesh is highly conductive and capable to transmitting a wide variety of types of energy, which allows the weapon to shock, cause intense pain, cause intense pleasure, or do a number of other things.

Core + Outer Layer: When the Rod is fully collapsed the core measures 3 inches in diameter & 12 inches in length, but it can extend to be up to 0.5 inches in diameter and 60 inches long depending on the base configuration:
   0.5 x 2.5 = 12in (1ft) Default Configuration "Dormant"
   0.6 x 2.1 = 18in (1.5ft) Rod Configuration
   0.9 x 1.4 = 24in (2ft) Tonfa/Nightstick Configuration "The Scepter"
   1.4 x 0.9 = 34in (2.8ft) Mace Configuration "The Mace"
   1.7 x 0.75 = 40in (3.3ft) Whip-Mace Configuration
   2.1 x 0.6 = 50in (4.1ft) Semi-Rigid Whip Configuration
   2.5 x 0.5 = 60in (5ft) Flexible Whip Configuration "The Coil"
Within each base configuration the Rod are dozens of settings that allow the Rod to take on a wide variety of shapes from beaded or ribbed to tapered to flared. In addition, there are dozens of other settings that allow the user to control the type & amount of energy produced by the Rod at any given moment or even control the temperature of the Rod as a whole (from 300f to -75f). Another common setting, when in melee combat against an opponent with a melee weapon is electromagnetic repulsion to protect the weapon from damage by bladed weapons. The energy most often used by wielders of the Rod however, is that causing great neurological pain to those struck by it. At the lowest settings the amount of pain delivered causes a moderate shocking/burning sensation and a seizing of the muscles, which then scales up to intense blinding pain with a high likelihood of causing unconsciousness at the highest. At any of these settings a biological creature with a central nervous system will take short-term damage, but it has no effect against anything lacking a central nervous system.

Handle/Hilt: The handle or hilt of the Rod is covered in the same black rubber-like material as the outer layer of the weapon but features a number of groves to increase the grip, and several embedded metal strips, as well as several barely perceptible raised bumps that serve as buttons. These buttons & embedded metal strips serve as the manual controls as well as the induction pads that allow mental control by a trained Domina. Each Disrupting Neural Stimulator is keyed to one specific individual through a combination of neural & DNA imprint, which prevents anyone other than its owner from activating or using it, but if the Domina has a cybernetic implant to link to the Rod, she may control every aspect of the weapon with a single thought, as if it were an extension of her own living body.
